<kml xmlns="http://www.opengis.net/kml/2.2"><Document><name>P098557 - Production</name><LookAt><longitude>-93.6176</longitude><latitude>41.5711</latitude><altitude>0</altitude><heading>0</heading><tilt>0</tilt><range>1700</range><altitudeMode>relativeToGround</altitudeMode></LookAt>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Line type (from the plan legend)</b>: solid = U.G. fiber in conduit / conduit path; dashed (drawn thinner) = U.G. IST. Aerial work (blue lines, strand, ANC &amp; DG) is not shown.<br/><b>Boxes</b>: square = new HH (handhole), FP (flower pot, 10x10 Round) or PED (pedestal). <b>Yellow circle = EXISTING HH/MH</b> (plan legend: EX. MH/HH DETAIL).<br/><b>Run labels</b> read: number of conduits x size SDR11 ORANGE, e.g. 2x 1.25" SDR11 ORANGE. Count comes from the plan callouts (BORE (1.25)PD ..., N CONDUITS); where the plan prints no count the run is 1 conduit (owner). Material per the BOM: 1.25" = INRDCT 1.25 SDR 11 ORANGE UG.<br/>Placement accuracy about +/-10 ft (plan sheets georeferenced to satellite imagery). Labels, box icons and plan callouts are hidden until you zoom in to street/block view; route lines stay visible at every zoom.<br/><b>Handhole / box sizes (plan callout -> spec name from the size reference):</b><br/>10x10  =  HH 10x10 ROUND SL ST<br/>12x12  =  HH 12x12<br/>17x30x24  =  HH 17x30x24<br/>30x48x36  =  HH 30x48x36 SPLIT LID NB<br/>13x24x18  =  HH 13x24x18 PL T22<br/>24x36x24  =  HH 24x36x24 SPLIT LID NB<br/>FP = 10x10 Round. PED = 8" or 10" pedestal. Existing MH 325: size not printed - PENDING CONFIRMATION. HH S5-HH-18 (SW 1ST ST at 1989/1991): no size printed on the plan or permit - PENDING CONFIRMATION.<br/>Box sizes were checked against permit ROWP-2026-002498 sheets B1-B7: the permit shows the same size at every box, so every size above is the plan size.]]></description>
