<Folder><name>Permit Requirements</name><description><![CDATA[Permit requirements from City of Des Moines ROW permit ROWP-2026-002498 (expires Nov 27, 2026). Highlights are drawn only on the permit-named streets that the route runs along; they and the labels appear only when zoomed in. Click a highlighted street or label for the permit text. Toggle this folder off to hide it.<br/><br/><b>PERMIT REQUIREMENTS - City of Des Moines ROW permit ROWP-2026-002498</b> (project PRJ12667; job P.098557)<br/><br/>Permit type: Right of Way - Excavation or Obstruction. Status: Issued. Issued: October 19, 2026. <b>Expiration: November 27, 2026</b>.<br/><br/>Site address (permit p.1): 1918 SW 2ND ST, DES MOINES, IA 50315. Work location (permit p.1): "Main Street: AOB; Cross Street Start: AOB; Cross Street End: AOB".<br/><br/>Available inspection (permit p.1): "Final Inspection - PDC Engineering".<br/><br/><b>Conditions (permit pp.1-2, quoted):</b><br/><br/><b>SPECIAL CONDITION:</b> "Special Condition - arrow board and peak hours restriction for any work along SW 9th St. Flagger and peak hours restriction for work along Hartford Ave/South Union St"<br/><br/><b>PEAK HOURS RESTRICTION:</b> "Work is not allowed in the roadway during the hours 7:00 AM to 9:00 AM and 4:00PM to 6:00PM."<br/><br/><b>ARROW BOARD REQUIRED:</b> "Electric flashing arrow board required."<br/><br/><b>PROFESSIONAL FLAGGER(S) REQUIRED:</b> "A partial or full lane obstruction on (Type Street Name) warrants a qualified flagger or flaggers be utilized when one lane in each direction cannot be maintained. Proof of flagger credentials must be provided on site during working hours. Off-Duty officers are available to use as a service for professional flaggers through the DMPD. Please contact Sgt. Anthony Ballantini at (515) 333-7134 to inquire for use."<br/><br/><b>MINIMUM LANES - Obstruct one lane only:</b> "Obstruct one lane only"<br/><br/><b>MINIMUM LANES - Maintain alternating traffic:</b> "Maintain alternating traffic"<br/><br/><b>WARNING SIGNS REQUIRED:</b> "48" X 48" Warning signs required."<br/><br/><b>Contractor Contact Information Required (permit p.1):</b> "24" X 24" signage containing contractor company and contact information is required to be posted on or near work site at all times."<br/><br/><b>TRAFFIC CONTROL DEVICES:</b> "All Traffic control devices used in conjunction with this work shall conform to and be installed as specified in the Iowa Manual on Uniform Traffic Control Devices and applicable city specifications."<br/><br/><b>SIDEWALKS CLOSED:</b> "Sidewalk on either side may be closed, with proper signs"<br/><br/><b>Plan-sheet notes (permit sheets B1-B7, CONSTRUCTION NOTES, quoted):</b> "1. LOCATE ALL UTILITY PRIOR TO DIGGING. ALL UTILITIES SHOWN ARE APPROXIMATE LOCATION ONLY." "2. POTHOLE ALL UTILITY CROSSINGS." "3. RESTORE ALL SURFACES TO ORIGINAL OR BETTER CONDITION." "4. POTHOLE ALL SERVICES IN THE WORK AREAS."<br/><br/><i>The permit states no work hours other than the peak-hour restriction above. The street names in the special condition are SW 9th St (arrow board) and Hartford Ave / South Union St (flagger). The permit work location is given only as "AOB". The peak-hours, lane, sign, sidewalk and traffic-control conditions are not tied to a street in the permit and apply as written. The permit cites Addendum 4 for approval; Addendum 4 is not in the PDF provided.</i>]]></description><Folder><name>Permit streets - highlight (Hartford Ave, S Union St, SW 9th St)</name><Folder><name></name><Region><LatLonAltBox><north>41.5701000</north><south>41.5679000</south><east>-93.6159000</east><west>-93.6181000</west></LatLonAltBox><Lod><minLodPixels>200</minLodPixels><maxLodPixels>-1</maxLodPixels></Lod></Region><Placemark><name>PERMIT - S UNION ST</name><description><![CDATA[<b>PERMIT REQUIREMENTS - City of Des Moines ROW permit ROWP-2026-002498</b> (project PRJ12667; job P.098557)<br/><br/><b>Highlighted street: S UNION ST</b> - The permit special condition calls for a flagger and the peak-hours restriction on this street.<br/><br/>Permit type: Right of Way - Excavation or Obstruction. Status: Issued. Issued: October 19, 2026. <b>Expiration: November 27, 2026</b>.<br/><br/>Site address (permit p.1): 1918 SW 2ND ST, DES MOINES, IA 50315. Work location (permit p.1): "Main Street: AOB; Cross Street Start: AOB; Cross Street End: AOB".<br/><br/>Available inspection (permit p.1): "Final Inspection - PDC Engineering".<br/><br/><b>Conditions (permit pp.1-2, quoted):</b><br/><br/><b>SPECIAL CONDITION:</b> "Special Condition - arrow board and peak hours restriction for any work along SW 9th St. Flagger and peak hours restriction for work along Hartford Ave/South Union St"<br/><br/><b>PEAK HOURS RESTRICTION:</b> "Work is not allowed in the roadway during the hours 7:00 AM to 9:00 AM and 4:00PM to 6:00PM."<br/><br/><b>ARROW BOARD REQUIRED:</b> "Electric flashing arrow board required."<br/><br/><b>PROFESSIONAL FLAGGER(S) REQUIRED:</b> "A partial or full lane obstruction on (Type Street Name) warrants a qualified flagger or flaggers be utilized when one lane in each direction cannot be maintained. Proof of flagger credentials must be provided on site during working hours. Off-Duty officers are available to use as a service for professional flaggers through the DMPD. Please contact Sgt. Anthony Ballantini at (515) 333-7134 to inquire for use."<br/><br/><b>MINIMUM LANES - Obstruct one lane only:</b> "Obstruct one lane only"<br/><br/><b>MINIMUM LANES - Maintain alternating traffic:</b> "Maintain alternating traffic"<br/><br/><b>WARNING SIGNS REQUIRED:</b> "48" X 48" Warning signs required."<br/><br/><b>Contractor Contact Information Required (permit p.1):</b> "24" X 24" signage containing contractor company and contact information is required to be posted on or near work site at all times."<br/><br/><b>TRAFFIC CONTROL DEVICES:</b> "All Traffic control devices used in conjunction with this work shall conform to and be installed as specified in the Iowa Manual on Uniform Traffic Control Devices and applicable city specifications."<br/><br/><b>SIDEWALKS CLOSED:</b> "Sidewalk on either side may be closed, with proper signs"<br/><br/><b>Plan-sheet notes (permit sheets B1-B7, CONSTRUCTION NOTES, quoted):</b> "1. LOCATE ALL UTILITY PRIOR TO DIGGING. ALL UTILITIES SHOWN ARE APPROXIMATE LOCATION ONLY." "2. POTHOLE ALL UTILITY CROSSINGS." "3. RESTORE ALL SURFACES TO ORIGINAL OR BETTER CONDITION." "4. POTHOLE ALL SERVICES IN THE WORK AREAS."<br/><br/><i>The permit states no work hours other than the peak-hour restriction above. The street names in the special condition are SW 9th St (arrow board) and Hartford Ave / South Union St (flagger). The permit work location is given only as "AOB". The peak-hours, lane, sign, sidewalk and traffic-control conditions are not tied to a street in the permit and apply as written. The permit cites Addendum 4 for approval; Addendum 4 is not in the PDF provided.</i>]]></description><styleUrl>#permit_line</styleUrl><LineString><tessellate>1</tessellate><coordinates>-93.6160000,41.5697745,0 -93.6160220,41.5697590,0 -93.6160410,41.5697080,0 -93.6160430,41.5688890,0 -93.6160440,41.5685530,0 -93.6160445,41.5682658,0</coordinates></LineString></Placemark></Folder><Folder><name></name><Region><LatLonAltBox><north>41.5701000</north><south>41.5679000</south><east>-93.6139000</east><west>-93.6161000</west></LatLonAltBox><Lod><minLodPixels>200</minLodPixels><maxLodPixels>-1</maxLodPixels></Lod></Region><Placemark><name>PERMIT - HARTFORD AVE</name><description><![CDATA[<b>PERMIT REQUIREMENTS - City of Des Moines ROW permit ROWP-2026-002498</b> (project PRJ12667; job P.098557)<br/><br/><b>Highlighted street: HARTFORD AVE</b> - The permit special condition calls for a flagger and the peak-hours restriction on this street.<br/><br/>Permit type: Right of Way - Excavation or Obstruction. Status: Issued. Issued: October 19, 2026. <b>Expiration: November 27, 2026</b>.<br/><br/>Site address (permit p